{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S101-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"609a08e569e0ebdcdf1056a63041f10afd1010380a7a5e272c56a606fcb9cb30\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims prior hardship; A3 judges B a beginner; A5 prescribes A's coping method.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 judges B2's immediate reading, but A5 answers B4's difference with a largely repeatable command.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants immediate information and B4 asserts an individual way of coping.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 intensifies the condescension after B4 without materially developing the tea prescription.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'failed opening' and reviews suggest a performance but leave the occasion indistinct.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'beginner's relationship' earns its condescension; A5's 'inventing suffering' is less concrete.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your first restaurant review? When mine came, I made tea before opening it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've opened it. Two stars. I'm ringing the critic.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's the stage where I unplugged my phone. Milk?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've already dialled.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then let it ring while the tea brews. You're rushing a mistake I took all afternoon over.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts having endured hardship first into authority to prescribe coping and grade B's reactions.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"S106 competes for greater sympathy through greater pain; S101 claims superior qualifications to guide someone else.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 calls B a beginner and A5 recommends A's method, making the claimed advantage instructional rather than a demand for sympathy.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now uses urgent practical intervention between restaurateurs; alternative b turns a departing colleague's good news into another mentoring opportunity.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original B4–A5 link repeated the prescription. The revision introduces a restaurant review and an imminent call. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 maps B's reaction onto A's coping history); logic 5 (B2's call prompts unplugging advice, B4's dialling prompts delay); relationship 4 (B2 and B4 pursue immediate contact); heightening 4 (A5 supervises an underway mistake); specificity 5 (A1 names the review); brevity 4 (A5's afternoon comparison follows the game). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 needs protective sincerity; a sneering delivery would reduce experienced guidance to generic superiority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S101-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"481f5510878d3ad8c2c494c5c83ec5d8713778f45159992f9c2702653beeae0f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes earlier redundancy as authority; A3 diagnoses optimism and A5 extends the advice.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 interprets B2's excitement; B4's new job makes A5 switch from leaving to starting over.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 correct A's assumptions without entering a contest over who suffered more.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands A's claimed expertise when B4 removes the presumed unemployment crisis.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's redundancy and slow desk tidying establish an immediately playable workplace departure.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Early stage' efficiently converts B2's happiness into evidence for A's diagnosis.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I went through redundancy before you. First, tidy your desk slowly.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm actually excited to leave.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Early stage. I recognise the optimism.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I have another job.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. You'll need my advice about starting over.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses prior hardship to claim continuing authority over how B should understand and handle a transition.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Pain competition would make B's redundancy an occasion to demand sympathy for A's worse experience.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 diagnoses B's optimism and A5 offers starting-over advice; neither turn asks B to attend to A's suffering.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b adapts mentorship to unexpectedly positive news; revised alternative a urgently regulates a specific risky reaction.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread: B4's new job genuinely redirects A5's guidance, preserving the card through a helpful development. The original coach-1.0 ratings stand; the five spoken turns satisfy the causal gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 names advice without giving it, so its specificity is weaker than the opening desk instruction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S102-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0f975e8b9c898b1a2e6db1a420f8083df355f7f525eb574335ea0e345e76ac55\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 politely suppresses hurt and A5 makes B's attention feel overdue, though A3 becomes conspicuously arch.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's disappointment diagnosis, but A5 treats B4's repair offer as if B had only just noticed.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers repair, yet A5 supplies no concrete way for that offer to change the relationship.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds another reproach after B4 without developing the ticket or the proposed repair.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 clearly establishes a forgotten concert and an unused ticket.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'amount of spare ticket' feels verbally manufactured beside A1's natural disappointment.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 65\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You forgot the concert. That's all right. I kept your ticket until the interval.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Let me take you next week.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's kind. I'll buy mine, and you can decide nearer the time.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll buy both. Put it in my calendar now.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Both tickets. How lovely. I'll put my name in the reminder too.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes restrained hurt and carefully limited trust motivate B to offer more than A directly requests.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Open guilt-tripping or sarcasm states the grievance aggressively instead of allowing restrained disappointment to exert pressure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1's 'quite all right' masks hurt; revised A3 lowers reliance on B, and A5's careful praise carries the remaining doubt.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a makes a forgotten outing produce increasing commitments; alternative b makes a late family call produce a smaller, more dependable promise.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original repair offer went unused. Internal reread of the revision, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3's reduced trust and A5's qualified praise); logic 5 (B2's invitation prompts separate tickets, B4's calendar prompts a named reminder); relationship 4 (B4 offers practical accountability); heightening 4 (A5 extends doubt into the reminder); specificity 5 (A1's interval anchors the loss); brevity 4 (A5's praise carries the sting). Total 92. Concert setting preserved; five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 can sound cutting if heavily emphasized; quiet relief mixed with doubt better preserves the instruction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S102-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"968a424592711e8ae6a532846a53d005473b1e05930bebe412ac8268933998d4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 explicitly lowers expectations and A5 offers cautious praise, although A1 announces the technique.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's hour and A5 responds to B4's proposed earlier call.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 briefly defends the lateness, then B4 supplies a repair without adding a meaningful constraint.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats lowered expectations after B4 rather than making the new promise consequential.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a promised call but no relationship or practical consequence; A3's resized hour is abstract.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'lowering my expectations gently' and A3's adjusted hour sound composed rather than conversational.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely to hear from you, love. I took the phone to bed at nine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mum, my shift ran late. I'll call at eight tomorrow.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Eight would be lovely. I won't keep the evening clear.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can promise ten minutes on my break.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Ten minutes. That's thoughtful. I'll save the important things.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A communicates hurt through modest expectations and careful appreciation that quietly increases the significance of B's promise.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply complaining about lateness would make an explicit demand; this card influences through the weight of what A appears willing to accept.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 calls an earlier call a 'pleasant surprise'; revised A3 releases the evening while A5 loads ten minutes with important matters.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b gives a working child a real time constraint and a parent restrained longing; alternative a negotiates trust through tickets and a calendar.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the abstract hour language with a family call constrained by shift work. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 lowers expectations and A5 carefully praises); logic 5 (B2's eight prompts A3's evening, B4's ten minutes sets A5's limit); relationship 4 (B2 explains work and B4 offers a feasible break); heightening 4 (A5 concentrates important matters into that break); specificity 5 (A1's bedside phone and B2's 'Mum'); brevity 4 (A5 implies the pressure). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final line may also express healthy prioritization; the earlier disappointment must remain audible without melodrama.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S103-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"82b0f73a0fbfc638b6ed034f34d1c74d57a410cda67b737f0fc9590159b33cef\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 revives their shared bookshop plan; A3 and A5 repeatedly return to its two chairs under present constraints.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's rent concern shrinks A3's proposal to chairs; B4's tiny flat makes A5 defer the sea.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 voice credible shared financial and spatial limits that shape A's hopeful compromise.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns A1's remembered aspiration into a present commitment to sit together despite B4's cramped flat.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's napkin plan, A3's drawn chairs and B4's tiny flat give actors a clear shared world.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Sea later. Chairs together now' compresses the practical and emotional compromise.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"This napkin still says we'll open a bookshop by the sea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We drew that before rent became real.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We also drew two chairs. We could start there.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"In our tiny flat?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. Sea later. Chairs together now.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A repeatedly uses a specific hope once shared with B to find emotional footing inside present limitations.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"S110 revives A's own earlier hopeful self; this card depends on a remembered aspiration belonging to both people.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1's 'we'll open' and A3's 'We also drew' establish joint history; A5 preserves togetherness rather than claiming personal fearlessness.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a extracts a livable piece from a large shared dream; alternative b restarts saving for the original shared trip.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B's rent and space objections successively reshape the same remembered plan, and A5 develops its emotional core. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand; the helpful compromise passes the causal gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The ending is tender rather than strongly comic, and its clipped phrasing may feel polished in casual performance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S103-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fb7f94205256889ecdf268762cc3fb9d74f345ebcf5b184f51e1468ac003b8c3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recalls the jar's shared summer-trip purpose; A3 and A5 preserve that hope after B2 reports the money gone.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes the idea from B2's spent money; A5 answers B4's request for a present contribution.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies a financial setback and B4 shifts into constructive participation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from A3's symbolic preservation to restarting the shared saving with one coin.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's jar of spare buttons makes the abandoned trip visible and playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'jar kept the idea' and A5's 'old job' sustain one economical image.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Remember when this jar meant a summer trip, not spare buttons?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We spent the money.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The jar kept the idea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What can we put in it today?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One coin. Let it remember its old job.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats the remains of a shared earlier plan as a place to return emotionally when present resources disappoint.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic optimism can propose any better future; this behavior specifically restores a hope A and B already held together.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks B to remember the summer-trip jar, and A5 returns that same jar to its previous shared purpose.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b recruits B into a tiny restart; alternative a accepts a changed version of the dream that fits their flat.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B4's invitation to contribute makes A5's coin a consequential cooperative step. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand; escalation is renewed commitment rather than conflict.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 is accommodating and the practical stakes are light; the coin produces a modest rather than surprising development.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S104-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6e2613aa328c36093f8be0759e3c177f8a00516ef0d14e2f744c6d37c21664ac\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes B's past scarf loan to earn honesty, and A3 values B's staying over fixing things.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly uses B2's inability to fix everything; A5 answers B4 but repeats A1's unspecified honest answer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 limits the rescuer role and B4 asks what support A actually needs.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates the demand for unprotected honesty without identifying a new consequence after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 specifies a scarf and a bad night but never establishes what present question B must answer.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's weather comparison economically distinguishes presence from repair, though A5 stays abstract.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You lent me this scarf when my marriage ended. Tell me honestly: should I answer his message?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can't decide that for you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You didn't decide anything that night. You stayed. Tell me what worries you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That you'll spend tonight waiting for another message.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then stay while I leave it unanswered. I'll make us tea this time.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats comfort previously received from B as an enduring bond that can now support honesty, patience and returned care.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"S107 depends on B's reassuring reactions to feel safe; S104 invokes a history of care as grounds for a continuing reciprocal bond.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 names the scarf loan and A3 recalls B staying; revised A5 adds returned hospitality after receiving B's honest concern.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a seeks candid advice about contact with an ex and then shared company; alternative b turns a former shopkeeper's request into support for B's own uncertainty.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a concrete present dilemma about an ex's message. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 invokes comfort, A5 reciprocates); logic 5 (B2's boundary prompts concerns instead, B4's waiting concern prompts leaving the message unanswered); relationship 5 (B2 limits responsibility and B4 offers specific honesty); heightening 4 (A5 asks for sustained company); specificity 5 (A1 names the decision); brevity 4 (A5's tea carries reciprocity). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The newly specified separation gives the scene emotional weight; it is a clear playable example with only gentle wit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S104-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"276b19a66c8453a38a39083ed16b3a9f6a3506f2679fd7c567588f5552549e9a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes B's support through the shop closing; A3 uses their shared silence to permit honest uncertainty.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 accepts B2's not knowing; A5 accepts B4's request to sit, although the original 'maybe' remains unexplained.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 cannot supply an answer and B4 offers presence, which A5 recognizes as valuable.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 validates the sitting offered in B4 but adds little beyond A3's permission for silence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's shop closure establishes history but not the present request receiving a 'polite maybe'.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'whole hours of it' makes silence concrete without a separate explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 78\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You sat with me when my shop closed. Will you help at the new stall? An honest answer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I don't know. My own shop's struggling.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then forget the stall. You let me talk for hours when mine went.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could we sit without talking first?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. You gave me three silent evenings. I've kept this one free.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses the memory of B's past comfort to establish a bond that now warrants candid answers and reciprocal patience.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Calling in a favor treats past care as a debt payable to A; this card also allows that history to generate care flowing back to B.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 permits B's uncertainty because they endured silence together; revised A3 releases the stall request and A5 returns that patient presence.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b reverses who currently needs support after B's disclosure; alternative a keeps A as the person in difficulty while adding a smaller reciprocal gesture.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified the unanswered request and gave B a present problem. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 turn past comfort into returned support); logic 5 (B2's struggling shop redirects A3, B4's silence sets A5's offer); relationship 5 (B2 reveals competing need and B4 chooses the support); heightening 4 (A5 commits an evening); specificity 5 (A1's new stall); brevity 4 (A5's counted evenings embody patience). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's availability is newly revealed and should sound like willing generosity rather than a suspiciously convenient prepared speech.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S105-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"90c0f0b46bc0f9e02365c1b8dc350c1cb00958373e48e7a804c176b11475569d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 serves everyone and volunteers for calls; A3 minimizes shaking; A5 resists B's offered care.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's shaking concern into a reason calls remain possible; A5 responds to B4's invitation to sit.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 notices A's physical strain and B4 offers to take over the actual task.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"After B4 removes the calling burden, A5 claims a further duty to appear in control.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's tea and difficult calls, followed by B2's shaking hands, establish an active domestic crisis.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's distinction between calls and trays makes the denial follow A's practical logic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've made everyone tea. I'll handle the difficult calls.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Your hands are shaking.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then it's good the calls don't require trays.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sit down. I'll call.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Someone needs to look like we're managing. I'll sit after that.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A protects the role of steady caretaker by minimizing visible strain and finding another responsibility whenever B offers relief.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary helpfulness accepts useful assistance; this card specifically resists becoming a recipient of care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 dismisses B2's evidence of shaking, and A5 postpones sitting even after B4 offers to make the calls.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a protects the group's appearance of competence through task management; alternative b redirects intimate comfort into caring for a distressed child.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B4's practical solution creates A5's new justification for remaining the strong one. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand, with five spoken turns and causal use of both B contributions.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The underlying crisis is unspecified, and 'I'll sit after that' depends on A sincerely treating visible steadiness as unfinished work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S105-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3708a8b87a129b7b34a4c854521ef9fe7df8eaf84fd87930a635f7fc08e03573\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives away the last tissue, A3 minimizes tears, and A5 redirects B4's care toward everyone else.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's observed crying; A5 inverts B4's offer but uses no specific form of proposed care.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 express concern but offer little personal need or concrete intervention for A to handle.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates the caretaker priority at a broader scale without a new practical consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a tissue and sleeve, but neither A1 nor B2 locates the shared tears in a situation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Efficiently' gives A's self-denial a compact resource-management logic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 78\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Take the last tissue. Mum's funeral was hard on you. I've got my sleeve.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're crying into both sleeves.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They're washable. How's your daughter holding up?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She's asleep. Come here. You can cry on my shoulder.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You'll need that shoulder when she wakes. I'll get you a dry cardigan.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A maintains strength for other people by discounting personal distress and converting offers of comfort into further caretaking.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Stoicism can simply conceal emotion; this card actively steadies others and resists their attempts to provide care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 gives B the tissue and A5 redirects B's care; revised A5 preserves B's shoulder for the child and supplies clothing.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses physical intimacy and family responsibilities; alternative a uses practical delegation and the appearance of collective control.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a funeral and a sleeping child to make care concrete. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 minimizes tears and A5 rejects comfort through service); logic 5 (B2's sleeves prompt washability, B4's shoulder prompts preserving it); relationship 4 (B4 offers physical comfort and resolves the child's current need); heightening 4 (A5 invents future caretaking grounds); specificity 5 (A1's funeral); brevity 4 (A5's cardigan follows the wet-sleeve problem). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The funeral setting makes the humor delicate; A's concern for B must remain real for the redirection to land.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S106-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"848b1058f68aeab7c8d59b3c32c894874d5d592b131d294029918c28e70f0ca9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 weighs B's single rejection against fourteen, A3 establishes a scale, and A5 claims time for A's pain.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's request for personal attention; A5 turns B4's rejection of competition into a claim on listening time.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to discuss this rejection and B4 challenges the comparative framework.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 converts A1's numerical comparison into an obligation to hear all fourteen stories.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's retained rejection letters give the emotional comparison a tangible count.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'establish the scale' exposes A's sincere measurement logic in a short reply.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One rejection? I've kept fourteen letters. I can lend you perspective.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I just wanted to talk about mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Mine establish the scale.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It isn't a competition.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then you'll have time for all fourteen afterward.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A measures B's disappointment against accumulated personal suffering to claim a larger share of emotional attention.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"S101 uses hardship as authority to guide coping; S106 uses it to establish whose feelings should occupy more space.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explicitly establishes a comparative scale, and A5 demands listening time for fourteen disappointments instead of offering a coping method.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a claims airtime through the number of rejection letters; alternative b uses the duration of unemployment to bargain for a larger hearing.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. A5 uses B4's noncompetitive principle to justify abundant attention to A, developing the original numerical game. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The inference from 'not a competition' to enough time for fourteen is self-serving rather than formally logical; A must believe it is fair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S106-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"13519411893504ca29f4a9e75daa05f9a49a561c4e6ef08ba0f66f97fdc67dbc\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 compares a week with a year; A3 preserves the twelve-month advantage; A5 minimizes B's suffering again.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's wish to finish, but A5's quieter-Tuesday comparison could follow many replies besides B4's request to listen.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 both ask to be heard, giving A little new pressure on the second exchange.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 sharpens the insult but repeats A1's duration comparison rather than changing its consequences.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's rough week and rough year never identify an actual disappointment or concrete situation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's quieter Tuesday is compact and card-related, though more detachable than A3's response.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've been unemployed a week. I've been out a year. This coffee should really be for me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I bought it so you'd listen to what happened.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll listen. Mine will take longer; there's twelve months to cover.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Ten minutes each. I've got an interview.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"An interview already? Then give me fifteen. You've started recovering.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns comparative suffering into an asserted entitlement to greater time and sympathy.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Experienced mentoring would use A's year without work to help B; this behavior uses the year to claim the coffee and more listening time.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 makes B's week smaller than A's Tuesday; revised A5 treats B's interview as grounds for reallocating sympathy to A.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b bargains over a fixed conversation window and B's improving prospects; alternative a demands cumulative attention for a stack of past rejections.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced unemployment, a purchased coffee and an interview deadline. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 allocate care by comparative hardship); logic 5 (B2's listening purpose prompts duration, B4's interview changes A5's allocation); relationship 5 (B4 sets a limit for a credible appointment); heightening 4 (A5 claims fifteen of the available twenty minutes); specificity 5 (A1's coffee and unemployment); brevity 4 (A5's recovery diagnosis earns the bargain). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's numerical fairness is intentionally distorted; the actor should pursue recognition sincerely rather than enjoy humiliating B.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S107-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a7f40f6eea3f5f145167a86d0cf974cb8be9167e87cac84cd6ea4d23378491dc\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 relies on B's reassuring face, A3 claims independence while preserving it, and A5 reacts to B's uncertainty.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's independence challenge with a conditional demonstration; A5 uses B4's uncertainty to protect the reassuring expression.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 encourages independence and B4 honestly limits what B can know about the letter.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 wants B's face insulated from B4's admitted ignorance, increasing A's control over the reassurance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a seated companion and an unopened letter with an immediately playable dependency.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's face 'hearing' B4's admission gives a compact physical expression to A's safety measure.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay seated while I open this letter. Your face looks reassuring.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You can open it without me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Certainly. Keep looking like that while I prove it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I don't know what's inside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You weren't supposed to let your face hear that.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A gauges safety through one particular person's expression while insisting that dependence is smaller than it plainly is.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic reassurance-seeking only asks for comfort; this card makes B's reactions the safety instrument and includes A's downplaying.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 claims to prove independence while requiring B's expression, and A5 treats a change in that expression as the problem.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a tries to preserve B's reassuring face despite uncertainty; revised alternative b becomes ready to act after B smiles and credits the furniture.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. Both B replies alter how A maintains the facial reassurance, and A3 supplies the necessary denial of dependence. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The letter's contents remain unspecified, and A5's personification needs a light touch to avoid sounding like a prepared joke.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S107-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"9b2f250a9bbff02676852cde66bc8ddde7401f8bc675084167f2195c0d0a6043\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 deny needing B nearby, but neither establishes B's reactions as A's measure of safety.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 denies B2's nervousness diagnosis and A5 responds with relief to B4's promise to stay.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 identifies the dependency and B4 accommodates it without a distinct reaction for A to interpret.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the viewing-angle excuse after B4, with little new commitment beyond satisfaction.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names 'the result' and seating but leaves the event and source of uncertainty undefined.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'emotionally practical' describes the evasion too explicitly, and A5 repeats its angle metaphor.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Sit beside me while I open the audition result. You've stopped smiling.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm squinting at the screen. You haven't opened it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Right. So nothing's wrong. Move closer; the text is small.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm smiling now. Whatever it says, we'll get lunch.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"There. I can click it now. This chair was the problem.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets B's visible reactions as evidence of safety, then attributes the resulting confidence to an ordinary practical adjustment.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wanting companionship during a result is broader than this card; the distinguishing behavior is using B's reaction as a gauge and minimizing its effect.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 shows relief from presence only; revised A1 notices a lost smile, A3 infers safety from its explanation, and A5 credits the chair.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b lets B's supportive smile produce forward action; alternative a resists B's honest uncertainty to preserve a reassuring expression.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified an audition result and made facial reactions causal. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 reads safety and A5 disowns the smile's effect); logic 5 (B2 explains the expression, B4's smile enables clicking); relationship 4 (B2 corrects the inference and B4 offers lunch); heightening 4 (A5 becomes willing to open the result); specificity 5 (A1's audition screen); brevity 4 (A5's chair excuse completes the denial). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 explicitly reports smiling because the example permits spoken turns only; performance may make that line feel slightly demonstrative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S108-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e1cf8b5ba7ac903666d532ebe8ae7c1cd606a2c176a2fd737f3046ad60740386\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 avoids harmless blue cups, A3 implies an unwelcome memory, and A5 excessively controls the remaining sightline.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 refuses B2's historical inquiry; B4's offer to put the cup away creates A5's more exact hiding requirement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 tries to understand and B4 offers accommodation, which A then makes more demanding.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes even the visible handle unacceptable after B4 agrees to remove the cup.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's breakfast cups and A5's plates and handle make the avoidance physically precise.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Nothing breakfast needs to revisit' withholds history economically; A5's handle carries the resulting excess.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 89\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could we use any cups except the blue ones today?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What happened with a blue cup?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Nothing breakfast needs to revisit.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll put it away.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Behind the plates, please. The handle's still looking this way.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A responds to a harmless reminder of old hurt by controlling increasingly small details of its presence.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"An arbitrary dislike or superstition could also avoid a blue cup, but this card roots the control in something painful returning.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 asks what happened and A3 refuses to 'revisit' it, connecting A5's excessive concealment to implied history.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a contains a reminder through visual concealment; revised alternative b protects a celebration through increasingly exact envelope handling.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B4's helpful removal directly generates A5's stricter requirement, making accommodation develop the game. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The old hurt is implied rather than identified, so a purely whimsical delivery could obscure the card's emotional basis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S108-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5adeb2b1608f30649fba08cc22938e996c424492885093bef0d808dc081e4162\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 avoids a yellow envelope, but B2 identifies a bill and no turn establishes an old hurt rather than present financial stress.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's bill to relocate it; A5 explains B4's wiping observation without changing the avoidance.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects A and B4 notices repeated wiping, but neither offers a consequential alternative.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the envelope's exclusion already requested in A1 and A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's yellow envelope beside a cake and B4's table wiping establish clear physical business.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'everything except the envelope' is compact but mainly restates A3's relocation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 53\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you move that yellow envelope away from my birthday cake?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a voucher from your sister.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. My eviction notice came in yellow. I'll find her a nicer envelope.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll take the voucher out and bin this one.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. Under the coffee grounds, please. I'll hold the lid.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A overmanages an innocuous present object because one of its details recalls an earlier hurt.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding a current bill can be ordinary financial anxiety; this card requires the harmless reminder itself to activate old pain.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original B2 makes the envelope a live bill; revised B2 makes it a gift and A3 explicitly ties its yellow color to a past eviction notice.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b combines protective helpfulness with ceremonial disposal; alternative a relies on guarded silence and hiding a cup's remaining handle.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the cake and yellow envelope, changed its contents to a harmless gift, and supplied the old association. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3's remembered notice causes replacement); logic 5 (B2's gift prompts a nicer envelope, B4's disposal prompts burial); relationship 4 (B4 preserves the gift while helping); heightening 4 (A5 supervises disposal); specificity 5 (A1's birthday cake); brevity 4 (A5's coffee grounds embody excess). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The eviction reference is direct exposition, though brief; the scene needs care to keep the humor in control of the envelope rather than the past loss.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S109-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f072d219cf591f67925212eb8201c77d488a341206d090e0152656ec66b962b8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 resentfully admires B's immediate opening; A3 preserves the image of courage; A5 wants to match B's speed.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 interprets B2's admitted fear as well concealed; A5 rejects B4's offered time in favor of B's example.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 reveals vulnerability and B4 offers patience, both credible attempts to reduce A's self-comparison.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's permission to wait prompts A5 to impose B's exact speed as a personal standard.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 places both people with rejection letters and different willingness to open them.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'hid it very efficiently' turns B2's reassuring admission into another enviable achievement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You opened your rejection letter straight away. Must be nice, being brave on demand.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I was scared too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You hid it very efficiently.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Take your time with yours.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd prefer to need exactly as little time as you.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A experiences B's emotional courage as a model to emulate and an unfair exposure of A's own hesitation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple envy wants B's advantage; this card specifically combines admiration for emotional bravery with resentment of the comparison it creates.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names bravery resentfully, A3 treats hidden fear as an achievement, and A5 wants to reproduce B's readiness.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a resists permission to proceed slowly and sets a competitive standard; alternative b accepts practice while resenting B's apparent ease.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B4's patience intensifies A's demand to match B rather than relieving it. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand and the dialogue remains causally connected.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Calling the unopened item a rejection letter presumes A already knows its outcome; it is coherent if opening means facing the details.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S109-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"79ff4c28dabca70eda1ddabe22a620dc6b13746a76015c4c53a7643424933b28\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 explicitly admires and resents B's disclosure; A3 makes even stumbling courageous; A5 accepts help with continued resentment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly revalues B2's stumbling, and A5 specifically responds to B4's practice offer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects the idealized account and B4 offers a collaborative route into A's own disclosure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from judging B's past bravery to accepting practice while extending the comparison into it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an unrehearsed emotional disclosure and B4 gives the pair a playable activity.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's demand not to make practice look easy follows directly from A3's admiration of imperfect courage.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You told them how you felt without rehearsing. I resent how impressive that was.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I stumbled over half of it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Even your stumbling looked courageous.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Want to practise with me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. Don't make practising look easy too.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A draws inspiration from B's emotional bravery while resenting ho